sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant picocli as picocli CommandLine
    participant SC as SetupCommand
    participant STS as AWS STS
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant CFSvc as CloudFormationService
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant SSM as AWS SSM
    participant FS as Local Filesystem

    Note over User,FS: baas admin setup -- needs the elevated BaasCliDeployerPolicy.<br/>Deploys the CORE stack only. cf-template-ci.yaml is deployed by hand.
    User->>picocli: baas admin setup [--region] [--aws-profile] [--mongo-uri]<br/>[--use-existing-vpc --vpc-id --subnet-id --sg-id]
    picocli->>SC: parse and bind options into fields
    opt --mongo-uri provided
        Note over SC: validate the URI contains a database name<br/>fail here -- a bad URI should not cost a stack deploy
    end
    SC->>FS: ConfigService.load()
    FS-->>SC: BaasConfig from ~/.baas/config.yaml
    Note over SC: apply --region / --aws-profile over config defaults
    SC->>STS: sts.getCallerIdentity()
    STS-->>SC: caller ARN
    Note over SC: prefix = lowercase(base32(sha256(arn)))[0:8]<br/>stackName = bucketName = "baas-" + prefix<br/>both are FIXED by the caller identity, not user-selectable
    opt --use-existing-vpc set
        Note over SC: require --vpc-id + --subnet-id + --sg-id, else exit 1
    end
    SC->>FS: load /templates/cf-template-core.yaml from the classpath
    FS-->>SC: template body

    rect rgb(255, 244, 230)
        Note over SC,S3: Collision pre-check. The bucket is DeletionPolicy Retain, so a previous<br/>teardown can leave it behind, and CloudFormation would then fail with an<br/>opaque error that never mentions S3.
        SC->>CF: describeStacks(stackName) -- stackExists?
        SC->>S3: headBucket(bucketName) -- bucketExists?
        alt stack absent BUT bucket present
            SC-->>User: explain the retained bucket, print recovery commands, exit 1
        end
    end

    SC->>CFSvc: createOrUpdateStack(stackName, template, params)
    Note over CFSvc: params: ResourceNamePrefix, UseExistingVpc,<br/>ExistingVpcId, ExistingSubnetId, ExistingSecurityGroupId
    CFSvc->>CF: describeStacks(stackName)
    alt stack absent
        CF-->>CFSvc: stack not found
        CFSvc->>CF: createStack(CAPABILITY_IAM, CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM)
        CFSvc->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackCreateComplete()
        loop poll DescribeStacks
            CF-->>CFSvc: status = CREATE_IN_PROGRESS
        end
        CF-->>CFSvc: status = CREATE_COMPLETE
    else stack in ROLLBACK_COMPLETE
        CF-->>CFSvc: status = ROLLBACK_COMPLETE
        CFSvc-->>User: IllegalStateException -- delete it first with<br/>baas admin teardown --stack-name X --yes
    else stack exists and is updatable
        CF-->>CFSvc: existing stack details
        CFSvc->>CF: updateStack(CAPABILITY_IAM, CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM)
        alt template unchanged
            CF-->>CFSvc: ValidationError "No updates are to be performed"
            Note over CFSvc: swallowed -- report "already up to date" and return
        else changes applied
            CFSvc->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackUpdateComplete()
            CF-->>CFSvc: status = UPDATE_COMPLETE
        end
    end

    SC->>CF: describeStacks() -- read stack outputs
    CF-->>SC: BucketName, SubnetId, SecurityGroupId, VpcId,<br/>RunnerInstanceProfileName, OperatorRoleArn,<br/>RunnerRoleName, RunnerRoleArn, S3BucketArn
    SC->>FS: ConfigService.save() to ~/.baas/config.yaml
    Note over SC,FS: only non-sensitive values are written to the config file

    SC-->>User: BaasCliOperatorRole created -- nobody can assume it yet.<br/>1. grant sts:AssumeRole + add a ~/.aws/config profile (see infra/README.md)<br/>2. baas config set --operator-profile NAME<br/>until then `baas run` uses the default credential chain

    alt --mongo-uri provided
        SC->>SSM: putParameter(/PREFIX/mongo/connection-string, SECURE_STRING)
        SSM-->>SC: PutParameterResponse
        SC-->>User: MongoDB URI stored in SSM
    else omitted
        SC-->>User: print the Atlas free-tier signup link, tell the user to run<br/>`baas config set --mongo-uri` and to update the Atlas IP Access List
    end
    SC-->>User: exit 0
